## Part 2: Metadata Fetcher (Cloudflare Worker)

The metadata fetcher fetches page titles, descriptions, and preview images for bookmarked URLs. Without it the app falls back to public proxies, which may be slower or blocked for some sites.

### Step 1: Create a Cloudflare account and Worker

1. Go to [dash.cloudflare.com](https://dash.cloudflare.com) and sign up (free tier is fine).
2. Click **Workers & Pages** in the left sidebar.
3. Click **Create Application → Create Worker**.
4. Name it `stash-metadata-fetcher` and click **Deploy**.

### Step 2: Add the secret token

1. In your Worker page, click the **Settings** tab.
2. Scroll to **Environment Variables → Edit variables → Add variable**.
3. Set:
   - **Variable name**: `METADATA_TOKEN`
   - **Value**: a long random string, e.g. `stash-secret-xyz-12345` (use a password generator)
4. Click **Encrypt**, then **Save and deploy**.

Keep this token value — you'll need it in Step 3 of Part 3.

### Step 3: Deploy the Worker code

1. Click the **Code** tab in your Worker.
2. Replace the template with the code below and click **Save and deploy**.

```javascript
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    const token = url.searchParams.get('token');
    const targetUrl = url.searchParams.get('url');

    if (!token || token !== env.METADATA_TOKEN) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Unauthorized' }), {
        status: 401,
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      });
    }

    if (!targetUrl) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'URL required' }), {
        status: 400,
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      });
    }

    try {
      const response = await fetch(targetUrl, {
        headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; StashBot/1.0)' },
        timeout: 9000,
      });

      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}`);

      const html = await response.text();

      const getMetaContent = (property) => {
        const match =
          html.match(new RegExp(`<meta[^>]+property=["']${property}["'][^>]+content=["']([^"']+)["']`, 'i')) ||
          html.match(new RegExp(`<meta[^>]+content=["']([^"']+)["'][^>]+property=["']${property}["']`, 'i'));
        return match ? decodeHtmlEntities(match[1]) : '';
      };

      const getMetaName = (name) => {
        const match =
          html.match(new RegExp(`<meta[^>]+name=["']${name}["'][^>]+content=["']([^"']+)["']`, 'i')) ||
          html.match(new RegExp(`<meta[^>]+content=["']([^"']+)["'][^>]+name=["']${name}["']`, 'i'));
        return match ? decodeHtmlEntities(match[1]) : '';
      };

      const titleMatch = html.match(/<title[^>]*>([^<]+)<\/title>/i);
      const title =
        getMetaContent('og:title') ||
        getMetaName('twitter:title') ||
        (titleMatch ? decodeHtmlEntities(titleMatch[1]) : '');

      const description =
        getMetaContent('og:description') ||
        getMetaName('description') ||
        getMetaName('twitter:description') ||
        '';

      const imageUrl =
        getMetaContent('og:image') ||
        getMetaName('twitter:image') ||
        '';

      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ title, description, imageUrl }), {
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      });
    } catch (error) {
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: error.message || 'Failed to fetch metadata' }), {
        status: 502,
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      });
    }
  },
};

function decodeHtmlEntities(value) {
  return value
    .replace(/&amp;/g, '&')
    .replace(/&quot;/g, '"')
    .replace(/&#39;/g, "'")
    .replace(/&lt;/g, '<')
    .replace(/&gt;/g, '>')
    .trim();
}
```

After deploying you'll see your Worker URL in the format `https://stash-metadata-fetcher.your-subdomain.workers.dev`. Copy it.

